Check PHP compatibility for a local project, Git repository, or Packagist package.
Test a specific PHP version or find the lowest/highest compatible version checked.

Usage:
  php-compat-check <source> <php-version> [options]
  php-compat-check <source> --min-php-version [options]
  php-compat-check <source> --max-php-version [options]
  php-compat-check --help
  php-compat-check --version

Sources:
  . | .. | ./path | ../path | /path    Local working files (read-only)
  vendor/package[:version]           Packagist package with optional constraint
  Git URL                            HTTPS or SSH repository URL
  local:<path>                       Explicit local directory
  package:<package>[:version]         Explicit Packagist package
  repo:<url> | repository:<url>        Explicit Git repository

Options:
  -h, --help                         Show this help and exit
  --version                          Show the executable's version and exit
  --source-version=<version>         Select a remote package constraint, tag,
                                     or branch; unavailable for local sources
  --version=<ref>                     Deprecated alias for --source-version
  --min-php-version                   Find the minimum compatible PHP version
  --max-php-version                   Find the highest compatible version checked
  --from-php-version=<version>        Set the lower bound for a version search
  --to-php-version=<version>          Set the upper bound for a version search
  --ignore-composer-php-version       Ignore the project's Composer PHP constraint
  --check-deps[=shallow|full]          Include production dependencies (default:
                                     shallow trusts compatible PHP requirements;
                                     full scans all production dependencies)
  --show-deps                        Show dependency versions and scan status
                                     with --check-deps
  --show-warnings                    Display PHPCompatibility warnings
  --scan-dirs=<dirs>                 Scan comma-separated directories/files
                                     (default: Composer autoload paths)
  --upgrade                          Pull the configured Docker image
                                     (wrapper only; local installation unchanged)

Local checks use current files and installed dependencies without modifying them.
Remote sources are cloned; --check-deps installs their production dependencies.
The wrapper uses Docker. Set PHP_COMPAT_CHECK_IMAGE to choose a different image.

Examples:
  php-compat-check . 8.1
  php-compat-check . --min-php-version
  php-compat-check . --max-php-version --to-php-version=8.4
  php-compat-check vendor/package:^6.0 8.1 --check-deps=full
  php-compat-check https://github.com/vendor/package 8.1 --source-version=v6.0.2

For a complete overview, see:
  https://github.com/zoliszabo/php-compat-check#readme
